==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~14 seconds<sup>90f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~14 seconds<sup>90f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 6~14 seconds<sup>180f~420f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Start the level by upgrading your [[Worker Cat]] to max level. When the enemies get near your base, spawn a couple of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]]. Once your Worker Cat is maxed out, wait for your money to fill up. Once you have a full wallet, send out all of your [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] at once (except for [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]]). After that, focus on spamming [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cats]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cats]].

When Teacher Bear appears, you can now start spamming Giraffe Cat, as his quick movement speed and fast attacks exploit Teacher Bear's high knockback count. However, if you don't use Giraffe Cat, you will need to instead rely on Dragons and Titans. Once you kill Teacher Bear, victory will be yours.

